## Root cause

This is a **packaging regression in `use-m@8.14.0`**, surfaced via the unpkg "bare" URL — not a transient CDN outage.

In `8.14.0` the entry file moved under `/src`. The published layout is now:

```
/src/use.js
/src/use.cjs
/src/use.mjs
...
package.json  ("default": "/src/use.cjs")
```

There is **no root-level `use.js` anymore**. So the long-standing bootstrap URL resolves like this:

```
GET https://unpkg.com/use-m/use.js
  -> 302 Location: /use-m@8.14.0/use.js
  -> 404, body: "Not found: /use-m@8.14.0/use.js"
```

Consumers (e.g. `@link-assistant/hive-mind`'s `use-m-bootstrap.lib.mjs`) fetch that URL and `eval()` the response body **without checking the HTTP status**. The 404 plain-text body gets eval'd:

```
<anonymous_script>:1
Not found: /use-m@8.14.0/use.js
    ^^^^^
SyntaxError: Unexpected identifier 'found'
```

Hence the misleading `SyntaxError`.

Verified today (2026-06-15):

| URL | Result |
|---|---|
| `https://unpkg.com/use-m/use.js` | 302 → `/use-m@8.14.0/use.js` → **404 "Not found"** |
| `https://unpkg.com/use-m@latest/use.js` | **404 "Not found"** |
| `https://unpkg.com/use-m/src/use.js` | **200**, valid JS |
| `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/use-m/use.js` | **200**, valid JS |
| `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/use-m/src/use.js` | **200**, valid JS |

## Recommended fix (package side, keeps `/src`)

Publish a patch (e.g. `8.14.1`) that restores a root-level entry **without moving anything out of `/src`** — add thin re-export shims at the package root:

```js
// use.js   (root)
module.exports = require('./src/use.js');
// or, matching the file's module format, re-export from ./src/use.js
```

…and the same for `use.cjs` / `use.mjs`, plus add them to the `files` array in `package.json`. That makes `https://unpkg.com/use-m/use.js` resolve again, so every existing consumer keeps working with **no change on their side**, while the source stays in `/src`.

(Alternatively/additionally, add an `exports` map so tooling resolves `use-m` and `use-m/use.js` to `./src/use.js`.)

## Workaround for projects already using use-m

Until a patched version is published, point the bootstrap at the explicit `/src` path and **guard the eval** (check `response.ok` + reject non-JS bodies, with a CDN fallback). Example, applied to `@link-assistant/hive-mind`'s `src/use-m-bootstrap.lib.mjs`:

```js
const USE_M_CDNS = [
  'https://unpkg.com/use-m/src/use.js',
  'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/use-m/src/use.js',
  'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/use-m/use.js',
  'https://unpkg.com/use-m/use.js',
];

const fetchUseMCodeFrom = async (url) => {
  const response = await fetch(url);
  if (!response.ok) {
    throw new Error(`Failed to fetch use-m from ${url}: HTTP ${response.status}`);
  }
  const code = await response.text();
  const trimmed = code.trimStart();
  if (/^not found/i.test(trimmed) || trimmed.startsWith('<')) {
    throw new Error(`Non-JavaScript body for use-m from ${url}: ${trimmed.slice(0, 80)}`);
  }
  return code;
};

const defaultFetchUseMCode = async () => {
  const errors = [];
  for (const url of USE_M_CDNS) {
    try { return await fetchUseMCodeFrom(url); }
    catch (e) { errors.push(e.message); }
  }
  throw new Error(`Unable to load use-m from any CDN:\n  - ${errors.join('\n  - ')}`);
};
```

The simplest one-line workaround for any consumer is just to change the fetched URL from `…/use-m/use.js` to `…/use-m/src/use.js` (or switch the CDN to jsdelivr). Verified locally: with this change `solve` boots past the bootstrap and `use('lodash@4.17.21')` loads correctly.

The two guards (status check + non-JS body check) are worth keeping regardless of the package fix, so a future 404/redirect can never again be silently `eval()`'d into a cryptic `SyntaxError`.
